Ooh, really bad luck there.

The best way to handle Rodney, I think, is with a wand of death, which
keeps the mischief he can perform to a minimum.  Wands of death,
although nerfed a bit since the demons lords and princes were made
immune to them, still come into their own in the end game against the
Wizard and two of the riders, and are well worth wishing for (or
blessed scrolls of charging).

So long as you get the worst cursing monsters out of the game (I almost
always genecide 'L') and take care of the Wizard quickly, then usually
you don't get a second curse before you have the chance to do something
about the first one.  Next time, consider dropping the bad and zapping
a Wand of Cancellation (which shouldn't be put in Bags of Holding
anyway) at it, which will nullify the curse but won't harm the bag's
enchantment.

