Well first off, understand that really the only person you have to
please is yourself.  Here at rgrn, we tend to have a fairly strict idea
of what constitutes ethical Nethack play, but when it comes right down
to it, it's just a game.

It's not like you're playing on a public server, it's your first
victory, and (this is most important) it *was* an accident.  I'd say
not to worry about it, you haven't lost any karma over the situation,
and even if you did, it'd have been replaced by your problem being an
object lesson to us concerning Windows' sneaky auto-reboot-after-update
behavior.

Of course, next time, you should be more careful.  It's generally a bad
idea to leave Nethack games on too long -- besides Windows rebooting,
there's also system crashes and power failures to endanger your game.
You generally don't risk anything by saving out.


